{
  "_comment": [
    "Template only, and named so Codex cannot mistake it for the real thing.",
    "`agentgit install` writes .mcp.json beside it with the NODE, NODE_FLAGS, MCP",
    "and REPO placeholders resolved to this machine.",
    "",
    "Absolute paths are unavoidable here. A plugin is loaded from a cache directory",
    "whose location is generated at install time, so nothing inside the manifest can",
    "name this repository relatively. NODE_FLAGS is resolved at install time rather",
    "than hard-coded because Node only strips TypeScript types unflagged from major",
    "23 onward, and the plugin has to run on the Node the user already has.",
    "",
    "plugin.json deliberately does NOT declare `mcpServers`. Component discovery",
    "finds .mcp.json at the plugin root on its own, and declaring the path would make",
    "plugin validation require the file to exist in the repository -- which it cannot,",
    "because it is machine-specific and generated.",
    "",
    "`cwd` is deliberately absent. A server pinned to this repository would answer",
    "every question about the wrong workspace. Left unset, the server inherits the",
    "Codex session's directory, which is the project being worked on. When that is",
    "still not the right project, every tool takes an explicit `workspace` argument,",
    "and the server says so in its error rather than guessing."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "agentgit": {
      "command": "{{NODE}}",
      "args": [{{NODE_FLAGS}}"{{MCP}}"],
      "startup_timeout_sec": 30,
      "tool_timeout_sec": 60
    }
  }
}
